    {
      "reason": "The page definition binds the status to the MyReviewDetail read on /data/detail, and the cross-department reading rules require each reported status to carry its source page, current role, selected object, query time and field meaning. These are compatible: one supplies the operation, the other the labelling duty.",
      "status": "covered",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "sourceId": "k_cc329ac0a1339c5635ee:p2"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "k_c0b2f5f8e4074708fa11:p5"
        }
      ],
      "followupQuery": "",
      "requirementId": "attribute_1",
      "requiredPoints": [
        "The status shown on the Application Details page comes from the application detail read for the selected record, not from the list, licence or payment views.",
        "Each reported status must be labelled with its source page and the object it describes."
      ],
      "missingEvidenceType": "none"
    },
    {
      "reason": "The cross-department rules require the query time to accompany each reported status; the payment binding states an offset-free timestamp must not be silently labelled UTC or converted with an assumed server timezone. The Licenses timezone evidence is scoped to a different page/field and does not override this for the application detail.",
      "status": "covered",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "sourceId": "k_c0b2f5f8e4074708fa11:p5"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "k_b3ad44544cf08e9d4f5a:p3"
        }
      ],
      "followupQuery": "",
      "requirementId": "attribute_2",
      "requiredPoints": [
        "The answer must state the time at which the status was observed (the query time of the authorized read).",
        "A timestamp without an explicit offset must not be silently relabelled or converted using an assumed server timezone."
      ],
      "missingEvidenceType": "none"
    },
    {
      "reason": "The page definition states the detail is entered from a permitted current list record supplying taskId, with a readiness assertion that a current non-null detail exists and its applicationNumber and taskId match the requested record; the user guide confirms opening a row from the list reaches the detail page. Read-only re-read, no write.",
      "status": "covered",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "sourceId": "k_cc329ac0a1339c5635ee:p0"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "k_cc329ac0a1339c5635ee:p1"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "k_1128977b019d0fe6f6c9:p1"
        }
      ],
      "followupQuery": "",
      "requirementId": "attribute_3",
      "requiredPoints": [
        "To refresh, re-open the matching row from the authorized application list so the detail page re-reads the current record.",
        "The refreshed detail must still match the requested Application Number and its mapped task before the status is trusted.",
        "Refreshing is a read-only re-read; it does not change any data."
      ],
      "missingEvidenceType": "none"
    },
    {
      "reason": "The cross-department rules state that application, content-material, inspection, complaint and payment/refund statuses describe different business objects, that a relation does not imply immediate agreement of all views, and that contradictory observations must remain visible until scope/version/time are reconciled. The page facts add that lifecycle status and approval position are distinct. No opposing clause found.",
      "status": "covered",
